 :reading
 "The fundamentals are not independent gaps. They are the input list of Q(o|pi) = A composed with B^pi applied to the belief, scored against C, over a policy index pi, and the F0 census found that pi (:machine-policy-carrier), B at the controlled grain (:controlled-transition-kernel), the belief-to-state map (:belief-to-state-distribution), the intermediate Q(s|pi) (:policy-conditioned-state-predictive) and C at outcome grain (:machine-preference-distribution) were each missing on both sides -- five inputs and the constructor itself, seven entries with the parameter kernels. FOUR OF THOSE FIVE STILL ARE. Pi is not: it moved :out on 2026-09-05 by row :F7, on a decision record in which two distinct complete cascades for one selected mission are constructed and scored, so the first step of the order below has been taken at the runtime and not in Lean. That is why the Q constructor has stayed missing through repeated audits: it is not one declaration that nobody wrote, it is a composition whose every argument is absent at the required grain. The parameter kernels are a second cluster, hanging off canonical EIG rather than off risk. THE ORDER THIS IMPLIES: name pi, then map belief into the model's state, then make B carry the action, and Q is then a definition rather than a research problem -- which is the order Q-interface-completeness.edn :work-order already gives, now with the reason for each step measured. That order is why :F7 came before :F1 slice 2 rather than instead of it: the carrier is named, and the belief-to-state map and the action-carrying B are the two steps still open before Q is a definition."

